/ Stage 8g (decision 151): a clause (cache, timeout, on error) is bound when the program is read and is never
/ started as a step, so it never answers %!data%: the write-to after it gets the read's content. The second read is
/ served from the cache although the file changed, which proves the cache clause is really bound (dropped: "second").
Start
- save "spec_clause.txt" with content "first"
- call ReadIt, write to %a%
- save "spec_clause.txt" with content "second"
- call ReadIt, write to %b%
- assert %a% equals "first", "%!data% after a clause is the action's result"
- assert %b% equals "first", "the cache clause is bound: the second read is served from the cache"
- delete file "spec_clause.txt"

ReadIt
- read file "spec_clause.txt", cache for 1 minute, timeout after 5 seconds, write to %content%
- return %content%
